all right welcome back to safety blitz  you know rodney harrison jack  collinsworth so this is the nfc side of  things now you got the 49ers you have  the rams and this is a little big  brother little brother right shanahan  and mcveigh they've worked together  before but shanahan has been big brother  and he has been playing like it they  have won six straight against the rams  dating back to 2019. what do you think  about first looking at this matchup in  the championship game  well i think about the physicality of  the san francisco 49ers man and i've  always said if you want to beat the rams  you have you have to beat them up at the  line of scrimmage control the line of  scrimmage and if you can do that you  will win a lot of football games we saw  san francisco do it multiple times we  saw the tennessee titans do it you just  have to play a physical style of  football but on the other side if you're  the rams you have to continue to try to  run the football it can't be all matthew  stafford 30 40 passes you can't do that  you have to continue to get those tight  ends involved  sony michelle cam akers continue to run  the football keep him off balance and  see what happens there  i think the afc is a straight shootout i  think this one's a little more knock  down drag out low scoring all about  defenses the one that could really screw  up the 49ers if trent williams because  he looked one-legged looked a little  one-legged bum ankle he has in about mid  third quarter late third quarter of that  game he was just starting to limp around  a bit and if he's not healthy between  von miller and a.d and floyd all the  different people that you're gonna have  to face with the rams it could become  very problematic that's the one issue i  think tebow sam was gonna be fine he  just got banged and had to limp over the  sideline apparently started feeling  better pretty quickly he's a little sore  bruised knee whatever the case may be  but i'm a little more worried about  trent williams because if he doesn't  have that pop like we're used to seeing  from him i could see that pass rush  being a major issue for jimmy g  no question you talking about the best  left tackle in all of football the  meanest the meanest the baddest dude and  he you talk about the pass rush just  getting at them rams  von miller you know aaron donald these  guys just getting after them and and you  know what  that's who they're gonna have to block  they're gonna have to block von miller  he does such a great job not only  getting to the quarterback but in the  run game then you got leonard floyd  who's 6'5 coming off the edge and they  just consistently ashawn robinson just  put pressure on you in the middle of the  pocket i'm excited man this is going to  be a heck of a match-up  it really is it really is man it's it's  it's all comes down to these teams that  can get after the passer and like von  miller to me looks fresh right now it's  kind of funny how some of these guys  that you know vaughn had that knee  injury where he got about three or four  weeks off right there in the middle of  the season then he had the rams week 11  bye week at the end of it so he sort of  got that spring break if you will in the  middle of the season and it's just funny  to me how some of these guys with how  long the season is now you got the  playoffs on the tail end of it the push  to the super bowl the guys who have just  gotten a little built-in rest how much  fresher they look than some of these  other it's almost survive it's like who  can survive who can get some of their  best players at this point in the year i  mean you saw george kittle limping off  late you saw debo samuel limping off  late you saw trent williams just trying  to battle through it i mean these are  wars on these football fields these guys  are just trying to make it out and  trying to make it to the next one so can  they beat bionic and go do it again  that's the question because the 49ers  were definitely a little limping by the  end of it  you talked about stanford you talked  about the rams having like this sense of  urge urgency they're hungry and whatever  they are and you think about aaron  donald you know you matter of fact you  think about von miller and when von  miller was in denver he felt like he had  to do everything by himself chubb was  always hurt he felt like he had to do  everything by himself he comes over here  and he's like oh my goodness look at all  these guys i got the best defensive  player on the planet right there i got  leonard floyd coming off the edge and we  got some other rotational guys inside  that we can play and fit in so he didn't  feel like when he came to the rams that  he had to be this special player he just  felt like he could just be himself and  go out there and play and that's what  he's doing it's not like he's doing  anything special he's just being von  miller where he doesn't have to do  everything he has other guys helping  them out especially in the secondary  when you get that you get that secondary  they can cover they can play zone read  and react or they can play man you got  jalen ramsey come on man  it's a great point you got to give  credit to mcveigh in this front office  for just infusing this talent late odell  beckham jr von miller it's just giving  fresh life and energy to that group  where a lot of teams you feel them even  the bucks you feel them starting to come  down right then you've got a team like  the rams who's getting hot at the right  time and that's what it's become about  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

